<title>POLAND: Rolimpex plans dividend for 1996.</title>
<headline>Rolimpex plans dividend for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food trader and producer Rolimpex SA plans to pay a dividend for 1996 but a decision has yet to be made on the amount, the firm's spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;I hope the situation will become more clear by the end of May,&quot; Bohdan Gornicki told Reuters, referring to the amount of the expected dividend.</p>
<p>He also said the company's net profit growth this year should at least match inflation.</p>
<p>Rolimpex, which made a net profit of 10.3 million zlotys last year, paid a dividend of 2.5 zlotys per share for 1995's profit of 40.7 million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
